<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>apark_jackal</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>
  <author><name>CellularSheaves.jl</name><email>adamkadosh@gmail.com</email></author>
  <description>
    Clearpath Jackal J100. The chassis, fenders and wheels are Clearpath's own
    meshes out of clearpath_platform_description, and the dimensions, masses and
    inertias come from that package's j100.urdf.xacro, so the 0.262 wheelbase,
    the 0.37559 track and the 0.098 wheel radius are the real machine's.
    Collision stays a box and four cylinders. The Jackal is a four-wheel skid
    steer with no castor: all four wheels are driven, two per side, through the
    one DiffDrive plugin, so the interface the sheaf bridge sees is unchanged by
    that -- a Twist in, an Odometry out, same topics -- and stays the same when
    the model is swapped for clearpath_simulator or for the hardware.
  </description>
</model>
